    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-8556-1",
        "name": "USN-8556-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that the Net::IMAP client in Ruby did not properly sanitize Symbol arguments passed to IMAP commands. A remote attacker controlling a malicious IMAP server, or able to influence command arguments, could use this to inject arbitrary IMAP commands via CRLF sequences. (CVE-2026-42258)  It was discovered that the Zlib::GzipReader in Ruby did not correctly ensure sufficient buffer capacity in the zstream_buffer_ungets function. An attacker could use this to craft a gzip stream that, when processed, could cause a buffer overflow, resulting in memory corruption and possibly arbitrary code execution. (CVE-2026-27820)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-27820",
          "CVE-2026-42258"
        ]
      },
      "timestamp": "2026-07-16T13:54:42Z",
